<article class="env-lemma" id="2C2B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2C2B">Lemma <span data-tag="2C2B">6.1.4.6</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a presentable $\infty $-category. Suppose that $f: U_{\bullet }^{+} \rightarrow V_{\bullet }^{+}$ be a map in $\Res (\calX )$ which exhibits $V_{\bullet }^{+}$ as the groupoid resolution generated by $U_{\bullet }^{+}$. Then $f$ induces equivalences $U_{-1} \rightarrow V_{-1}$ and $U_{0} \rightarrow V_{0}$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\cDelta ^{ \leq 0}_{+}$ be the full subcategory of $\cDelta _{+}$ spanned by the objects $\Delta ^{-1}$ and $\Delta ^0$. Let $j: \cDelta ^{\leq 0}_{+} \rightarrow \cDelta _{+}$ denote the inclusion functor, let $j^{\ast }: \calX _{\Delta _{+}} \rightarrow \calO _{\calX }$ be the associated restriction functor. We wish to show that $j^{\ast }(f)$ is an equivalence. Equivalently, we show that for every $W \in \calO _{\calX }$, composition with $j^{\ast }(f)$ induces a homotopy equivalence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calO _{\calX }}( j^{\ast } V_{\bullet }^{+}, W ) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calO _{\calX }}( j^{\ast } U_{\bullet }^{+}, W ). \]
</div>
    <p>
      Let $j_{\ast }$ be a right adjoint to $j^{\ast }$ (a right Kan extension functor). It will suffice to prove that composition with $f$ induces a homotopy equivalence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calX _{\Delta _{+}}}( V_{\bullet }^{+}, j_{\ast } W ) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calX _{\Delta _{+}}}( U_{\bullet }^{+}, j_{\ast } W ). \]
</div>
    <p>
       The augmented simplicial object $j_{\ast } W$ is a Čech nerve, so that the underlying simplicial object of $j_{\ast } W$ is a groupoid by Proposition <a href="/tag/DEC8" data-tag="DEC8">6.1.2.11</a>. We now conclude by applying Lemma <a href="/tag/7930" data-tag="7930">6.1.4.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>